{"sequence":47,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T10:53:23.864436763Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-dd96264b","body":"In `run_probe_biofilter_scaling_bigger_media_faster_cycling_with_suffix`, the `biofilter_filter_area` check error message says \"2× media should expand filter habitat area by >1.5×\" but the actual media configuration is 500 cm² vs 4000 cm² (8× difference, not 2×). Fix the diagnostic string to say \"8× media\" or \"larger media\" so a developer seeing a failure isn't misled about the test setup.","dedup_key":"c36cf97ac97c5a1108bff517d01efdb280bc30b3df9030f04f2b36d46d00b171","run_id":"run-20260330083637","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":48,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T10:53:23.873400022Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-703dc756","body":"The substrate redox probe (probe 4) intentionally enables aeration for the inert control arm (`state.hardware.aeration.enabled = true; state.hardware.aeration.intensity = 0.6;` at line ~1167) but not the planted arm. The doc comment says it validates 'substrate geometry and root-zone effects' but the aeration asymmetry means it actually validates the combined effect of substrate geometry + DO regime. Add a brief note in the doc comment acknowledging that the two arms differ in aeration, and explain that this strengthens the test: even with higher DO, the thin inert substrate cannot sustain denitrification because it lacks sufficient suboxic volume.","dedup_key":"247c7a43376f283ead5152229cc72a3ce51121b0f0daa438dffa319f932c41ce","run_id":"run-20260330083637","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
